{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":120713,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0a8f7b13-762c-4760-8c5f-985a331c861c","total_cost_usd":0.7449220000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":43328,"cache_read_input_tokens":20164,"output_tokens":10881,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":43328,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":10881,"cache_read_input_tokens":20164,"cache_creation_input_tokens":43328,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":43328},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":29440,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.029525000000000003,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":10881,"cacheReadInputTokens":20164,"cacheCreationInputTokens":43328,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7153970000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"debris-designer\",\n  \"size_classes\": {\n    \"small\": {\n      \"slots_crushed\": 1,\n      \"slots_uncrushed\": 2,\n      \"hand_tetherable\": true\n    },\n    \"medium\": {\n      \"slots_crushed\": 2,\n      \"slots_uncrushed\": 4,\n      \"hand_tetherable\": true\n    },\n    \"oversized\": {\n      \"slots_crushed\": 6,\n      \"slots_uncrushed\": 12,\n      \"hand_tetherable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  \"debris\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"bent_truss_section\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Bent Truss Section\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 34,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 8,\n      \"notes\": \"A buckled length of lattice strut off a launch adapter; the suborbital band's only medium, kept medium on purpose so the player meets the four-uncrushed-slot cost while the haul it spoils is still cheap.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scorched_hull_plate\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Scorched Hull Plate\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 12,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 15,\n      \"notes\": \"Curved skin panel with one edge already burned brown by a pass it survived; the most common thing in the sky and the piece the player learns the hand magnet on.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"spent_booster_ring\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Spent Booster Ring\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 28,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 6,\n      \"notes\": \"The interstage collar left when somebody else staged; a flat ring of solid metal that stacks against the hold wall, so it is the heavy small that reads instantly as the same part the player just threw away.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"tangled_wiring_loom\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Tangled Wiring Loom\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 6.5,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 13,\n      \"notes\": \"A knot of harness cable and connectors; nearly free to tow, which makes it the piece worth grabbing on the way past rather than the piece worth crossing for.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cracked_antenna_dish\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cracked Antenna Dish\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 9,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 4,\n      \"notes\": \"A dented comms dish that still glints on its slow tumble; the player's first fragile piece, cheap enough in mass that the lesson costs only patience.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"insulation_blanket_wad\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Insulation Blanket Wad\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 4,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"Balled-up gold foil MLI, almost weightless on the tether; the piece that proves slot cost and mass cost are different currencies.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fairing_shard\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Fairing Shard\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 8,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"A composite splinter of nose cone with the paint still on it; easy filler that keeps a light run from coming home empty.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"camera_optics_pod\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Camera Optics Pod\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 5.5,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 3,\n      \"notes\": \"An intact imaging head with the lens somehow unbroken; light, delicate, and the cheapest possible rehearsal for the glass the player will chase higher up.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"derelict_upper_stage\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Derelict Upper Stage\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 180,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 1,\n      \"notes\": \"A dead kick stage tumbling end over end; crane-cable only, so it hangs there all semester as a visible promise of a tool the player does not own yet.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"satellite_bus_frame\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Satellite Bus Frame\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 62,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"The gutted skeleton of a comms satellite; the low band's staple and the first piece heavy enough that a second tether visibly changes how the jetpack answers.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"reaction_wheel_housing\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Reaction Wheel Housing\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 48,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 11,\n      \"notes\": \"A sealed flywheel can, dense for its size and still faintly spinning; solid enough to shrug off a bad landing, which makes it the safe half of a mixed haul.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cracked_solar_array\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cracked Solar Array\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 22,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 5,\n      \"notes\": \"A folded wing of cells with a spiderweb fracture across one panel; the signature fragile prize of the shipping slice — light to tow, ruinous to land hard.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fuel_tank_bladder\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Fuel Tank Bladder\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 18,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 12,\n      \"notes\": \"A collapsed propellant bladder still weeping frozen hydrazine; compact, forgiving, and the low band's answer to a hold with one slot left.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"gyro_package\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Gyro Package\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 26,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"A machined inertial unit the size of a toolbox and heavier than it looks; the piece that teaches, inside the shipping slice, that small is a slot cost and not a mass promise.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"star_tracker_head\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Star Tracker Head\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 11,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 3,\n      \"notes\": \"A baffled optical head that catches the sun on a slow cycle; small, precious, and usually parked out on its own orbit a real burn away from the clump.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"thruster_quad_cluster\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Thruster Quad Cluster\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 55,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 8,\n      \"notes\": \"Four scorched RCS nozzles on a common manifold; heavy, tough, and the load the player is towing when they first feel a cable come taut on a turn.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"dish_reflector_petal\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Dish Reflector Petal\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 19,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 2,\n      \"notes\": \"A mesh reflector segment that never folds flat and never crushes; light on the tether but it eats four uncrushed slots, so taking it is a decision about the hold, not the jetpack.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"collapsed_boom_mast\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Collapsed Boom Mast\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 260,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 1,\n      \"notes\": \"A telescoping mast jammed half-extended, longer than the rocket; crane-cable only, and the practice rendezvous for the capstone if the crane ever ships.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rtg_core_shell\",\n      \"display_name\": \"RTG Core Shell\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 96,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"A shielded isotope generator casing, still warm to the glove; the high band's workhorse and the clearest statement that up here the good stuff fights you on the way down.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"tungsten_ballast_slug\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Tungsten Ballast Slug\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 55,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"A trim mass the size of a brick and the weight of a full toolbox; one crushed slot, the densest thing per slot in the catalog, and still enough on its own to push a chute descent toward the hard-landing line.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"shattered_optics_mirror\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Shattered Optics Mirror\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 44,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 6,\n      \"notes\": \"A primary mirror segment with a crazed coating that throws light every few seconds; the glint the player sees from a band away and has to talk themselves into.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cryo_tank_segment\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cryo Tank Segment\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 78,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"A vacuum-jacketed tank barrel frosted white; solid, dense, and exactly the ballast that turns a one-pass reentry into a three-pass one.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ion_engine_gridset\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Ion Engine Gridset\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 21,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 5,\n      \"notes\": \"Paper-thin accelerator grids in a scorched frame; the lightest thing in the top band and the easiest of its prizes to lose to a hot pass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"hardened_avionics_core\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Hardened Avionics Core\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 52,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"A rad-hard flight computer in a milled block of aluminium; the reliable high-band pickup for a player who already knows the ride home is going to be ugly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"deep_space_dish_array\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Deep Space Dish Array\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 58,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 4,\n      \"notes\": \"A rigid high-gain antenna the size of a door; fragile, uncrushable, and heavy — bulk, mass and risk in one piece, which is the top band's whole argument.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"sensor_boom_assembly\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Sensor Boom Assembly\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 68,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"An instrument arm with three magnetometer heads still bolted on; awkward on the tether, and it swings wide on every direction change the player rushes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"armstrongs_satellite\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Armstrong's Satellite\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 350,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 1,\n      \"notes\": \"The one Mr. Armstrong lost on cascade day, parked above the top band — unique rather than spawned, fragile and oversized so it can only be craned, can never be crushed, and arrives broken unless the touchdown is soft; the heaviest single object in the game.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"band_summary\": [\n    {\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"piece_count\": 9,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.1,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 31.89\n    },\n    {\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"piece_count\": 9,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.167,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 57.89\n    },\n    {\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"piece_count\": 9,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.25,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 91.33\n    }\n  ],\n  \"revision_notes\": [\n    \"Finding 1 accepted. armstrongs_satellite drops from 480 to 350 kg, the top of the range the Economy Balancer asked for. At the mass scale the catalog implies (dry 45 kg, Storage tier 2 loaded with low-band junk), 350 kg is roughly the mass of a fully upgraded fully laden ship rather than ten times a bare one, so GDD 2.3.7's 'roughly doubles the ship's mass on its own' becomes true of the ship that will actually fly the capstone run. It remains fragile, oversized, uncrushable and unique.\",\n    \"Consequence of finding 1, declared rather than quiet. collapsed_boom_mast drops from 330 to 260 kg. Nothing was wrong with 330 on its own, but with the satellite at 350 a routine low-band oversized piece would have sat within 20 kg of the capstone, and GDD 2.3.7 requires the satellite to be unambiguously the heaviest object in the game. 260 kg keeps the boom mast the second-heaviest thing in the sky and a real crane rehearsal, with a 90 kg gap to the prize. This is the only piece I touched that no finding named.\",\n    \"Finding 2 accepted, with the size class kept. tungsten_ballast_slug drops from 84 to 55 kg and stays small. Lowering the mass was the Balancer's first option and it is the one that preserves the teaching: at 55 kg in one crushed slot the slug is still the densest piece per slot in the catalog (55 kg/slot against rtg_core_shell's 48 and hardened_avionics_core's 52), still heavier than the medium cracked_solar_array at 22 kg, and still enough to spoil a chute descent by itself. Moving it to medium would have deleted the lesson entirely; a pathological twelve-slug hold now weighs 660 kg instead of 1008, which is inside the range a Parachute tier can be tuned against.\",\n    \"Finding 3 partly accepted. spent_booster_ring moves from medium to small at the same 28 kg — a flat interstage collar stacking against the hold wall is honest fiction for a small, and it frees the suborbital band's second medium out of a 6-slot hold that cannot afford two of them. bent_truss_section stays medium, deliberately: the shipping slice needs the player to meet the medium class and the four-uncrushed-slot cost somewhere cheap, and the truss is the piece whose entire job is teaching that a medium is a decision about the hold. The other two levers the Balancer named — the tier-1 crush rule and the medium slot cost — are GDD 2.3.4 constants and not mine to move either, so size class was the only knob I had, and I turned it once rather than twice.\",\n    \"No ids were renamed, added or removed; the catalog is the same 27 pieces, 9 per band, with four mass changes and one size-class change. band_summary was recomputed from the array after the edits, not carried forward.\"\n  ],\n  \"design_notes\": [\n    \"Mass still carries the difficulty curve, because the Researcher established that altitude cannot: entry speed spans only 151-164 m/s across the three bands, a 1.27x heat ratio, so the return leg gets harder only if the cargo gets heavier. After this revision band mean mass runs 31.89 / 57.89 / 91.33 kg, a 2.9x climb from bottom to top; excluding the single oversized outlier in each band, the hand-tetherable population averages 13.38 / 32.63 / 59.00 kg, a 4.4x climb. Trimming the satellite and the slug flattened the top band by about 16% and the low band by 12%, both entirely in the oversized and post-semester pieces — no shipping-slice tetherable mass changed at all, so nothing already tuned against the suborbital or low bands has moved.\",\n    \"Fragile fraction is spawn-weighted, not counted, and is unchanged by this revision: suborbital is 7 of 70 weight (0.100) across 2 of 9 pieces, low is 10 of 60 (0.167) across 3 of 9, high is 16 of 64 (0.250) across 4 of 9. Fragile types keep below-average weights within their band so that adding a fragile type raises variety without inflating how often the player meets one.\",\n    \"Size class is authored against the fiction, never derived from mass, and the catalog still proves that to the player twice over: tungsten_ballast_slug is small at 55 kg and gyro_package is small at 26 kg, while cracked_solar_array is medium at 22 kg. Demoting spent_booster_ring to small at 28 kg strengthens rather than weakens this — it is now a suborbital small that outweighs a low-band medium. A slot is volume and a kilogram is handling, and the catalog refuses to let those two collapse into one number.\",\n    \"The shipping slice is complete without the crane and is untouched by this pass. Suborbital and low each contain small, medium and fragile pieces, so every rule the player must learn is teachable below 400 m. The three oversized pieces sit one per band at 180, 260 and 350 kg on spawn weight 1 each, marked crane-only so the slice can ship with them visible and unreachable.\",\n    \"Suborbital now runs 7 small, 1 medium, 1 oversized. That is one medium fewer than before and it is a direct answer to the Economy Balancer: a starting 6-slot hold with a tier-1 compactor can fill itself entirely on crushed smalls, meet exactly one medium, and pay four uncrushed slots for it as a deliberate lesson rather than as the default every run. Low and high keep 5 mediums of 9 apiece, so slots still fill faster with altitude, which is what GDD 2.3.7 asks for.\",\n    \"Fragile stays concentrated where reach cost is highest: cracked_antenna_dish and camera_optics_pod are the cheap suborbital rehearsals, star_tracker_head and dish_reflector_petal are the low-band decisions, and shattered_optics_mirror, ion_engine_gridset and deep_space_dish_array are the top-band prizes. deep_space_dish_array remains the deliberate worst case among tetherable junk — fragile, medium, and 58 kg — so the top band always offers at least one piece that is bulk, mass and risk at once.\",\n    \"No piece is strictly dominant after the revision. The heaviest tetherable pieces are non-fragile and crushable (rtg_core_shell, cryo_tank_segment, sensor_boom_assembly), the lightest are cheap filler, the densest-per-slot piece is a non-fragile small that punishes the landing, and every fragile piece pays uncrushed slot cost forever — so a greedy hold and a valuable hold are still different hauls, and the player still has to choose which one to fly home.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":54843,"ttft_stream_ms":3763,"time_to_request_ms":441,"type":"result","duration_ms":119579,"uuid":"26041bdf-bd37-4177-aedd-690c83fabb24"}
